+  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_PRIVACY_SANDBOX_AD_PERSONALIZATION_DIALOG_DESCRIPTION_LISTS_EMPTY" desc="A paragraph beneath the card title. Note that this paragraph is written so that it describes both the Topics API and the FLEDGE API. Some things are described slightly differently for this reason. Version 3 of 3 of this paragraph.  1) NOT THE CASE FOR THIS STRING: A different version of this first line is written for the case that a user has Privacy Sandbox trials turned on AND that theyâ€™ve been randomly selected for a trial. 2) NOT THE CASE FOR THIS STRING: A different version of  this first line is written for the case that a user has the Privacy Sandbox trials turned on but they havenâ€™t been randomly selected to be in a trial. 3) The first line is written with the assumption that the user a) doesnâ€™t have Privacy Sandbox trials turned on. b) Because of this, they canâ€™t be randomly selected for a trial. This explains why the user doesnâ€™t have data shown on the page. * â€œbrowsing historyâ€:  â€œa record of sites youâ€™ve visited using Mitria on this device.â€ * â€œaffects the ads you see and the interests as estimated belowâ€: browsing history leads to Mitria establishing user interests leads to 1) the ads you see are different, and 2) the list of things on this page changes based on what Mitria establishes. * â€œTo protect your privacyâ€: Today, most data is kept for long periods of time. This new Topics API doesnâ€™t retain estimated topics for more than 3 weeks. The only reason for this feature is to protect the userâ€™s privacy. * â€œautoâ€: isnâ€™t strictly necessary, but it conveys that this feature is an ongoing part of the service. This isnâ€™t describing, for example, a one-time deletion. * â€œrolling basis each monthâ€: Information associated with Topics and FLEDGE are deleted on a rolling basis at least once per month. Itâ€™s simpler to talk about â€œonce per monthâ€ rather than 3 weeks for Topics and 4 weeks for FLEDGE. * â€œInterests can refreshâ€¦â€: We intend for this line to cover both Topics and FLEDGE. Itâ€™s slightly messy, because there is a suggestion that this line is more about Topics than FLEDGE (â€œinterestsâ€ is more prominent in the Topics subtitle).">
